# touchLevel(Player player, Int level)
# Moves this player's play clock onto `level`, banking the time already spent
# on whatever level the clock was previously sitting on. Pass -1 to stop the
# clock (the player has left the jump area entirely).
#
# Every event that proves the player is still working on a jump - a fall, an
# ender pearl retry, arriving from the menu, touching the gold block - calls
# this, so the gap since the previous such event is banked into
# levelTimes[previous].
#
# Two guards keep the number honest:
#   * A gap longer than idleCapMs is CLAMPED, not discarded. The old
#     timeOfLastFall logic threw away any gap over 60s outright, which is why
#     jumps beaten in one or two tries recorded no time at all and slow jumps
#     silently lost their longest attempts. Clamping keeps a genuinely slow
#     attempt while stopping an AFK or a logout from adding hours to a jump.
#   * Time is only banked for jumps the player has NOT beaten yet, matching
#     levelFalls and levelTeleports. These stats describe first clears, so
#     messing about on a jump you already beat must not change its difficulty.

@using j100
@fast

@define Long now = system::currentTimeMillis()
@define Int previous = currentLevel[player]
@define Long elapsed = 0L

@if previous >= 0 && levelClockStart[player] > 0L && levelsCompleted[player][previous] == false
    @var elapsed = now - levelClockStart[player]
    @if elapsed > idleCapMs
        @var elapsed = idleCapMs
    @fi
    @if elapsed > 0L
        @var levelTimes[player][previous] += elapsed
    @fi
@fi

@var currentLevel[player] = level

@if level >= 0
    @var levelClockStart[player] = now
@else
    @var levelClockStart[player] = 0L
@fi
